2026-09-26 — K02f: select existing scalar shift immediates.

RED: the MIR immediate-shape assertion and CLI assembly assertion fail, with
zero compilation errors. The C program's numeric result already agrees.
GREEN: decode a directly known count at its own bits<M> width (M <= 64), and
select lsl/lsr/asr #imm only when it is below the shifted width N <= 64.
All source UB guards, sign/zero extension and dynamic/pair paths remain intact.
This is instruction selection, not a new EqSat rule or source-language policy.

Four MIR tests: 90 defined selection cases, 450 exact EvoIR/MIR comparisons, 36 dynamic/
out-of-range controls, four original E3005 traps and 60 Linux/Darwin assembler
checks. The existing 28 lowering tests retain narrow operand extensions and
now also explicitly check their dynamic count masks. One CLI test passes at
O0/O2 through C-HIR, EvoIR, MIR and native assembly selection.
